*{{audio|en-us-ain't.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Contraction===
{{smarter|isn't|aren't|haven't|doesn't}}
'''ain’t'''

# {{slang}} [[are|Are]] [[not]], [[aren't|aren’t]]; [[is]] not, [[isn't|isn’t]]; [[am]] not.
# {{slang}} [[have|Have]] not, [[haven't|haven’t]]; [[has]] not, [[hasn't|hasn’t]].
# {{cattag|slang|some dialects}} [[do|Do]] not, [[don't|don’t]]; [[does]] not, [[doesn't|doesn’t]]; [[did]] not, [[didn't|didn’t]].

====Usage notes====
*This word is still considered an [[illiteracy]] and can stigmatize the user as ignorant.

===Quotations===
*'''1885''' — [[w:Gilbert and Sullivan|Gilbert & Sullivan]], ''[[s:The_Mikado|The Mikado]]''
*:We figure in lively paint -
*:Our attitude’s queer and quaint —
*:You’re wrong if you think it '''ain’t''', oh!

